        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes: toggle is \"split if on single line, join otherwise\". Doing `toggle` twice [is documented](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/46774982c5b74ca056e640aa92689f26f9c62139/doc/mini-splitjoin.txt#L40-L41).\r\n\r\nUsing `split` explicitly won't actually work here at the moment (and I doubt it will), as I have hard time finding a universal rule on when and how to split when arguments are not on the same line.",
            "created_at": "2023-03-10T14:35:50Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/260#issuecomment-1463892945",
